.\" DO NOT MODIFY THIS FILE!  It was generated by help2man 1.49.3.
.TH SMBIOS-TOKEN-CTL "1" "December 2025" "smbios-token-ctl 2.4.3" "User Commands"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
smbios-token-ctl \- ../src/bin/smbios-token-ctl
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.B smbios-token-ctl

.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dump\-tokens\fR
Action: dump token table
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-tokens\-csv\fR
Action: dump token table in CSV format
.TP
\fB\-\-import\-token\-settings\-csv\fR
Action: Restore token settings from CSV table dump
.TP
\fB\-\-is\-string\fR
Action: return true if specified token is a string.
.TP
\fB\-\-is\-bool\fR
Action: return true if specified token is a bool.
.TP
\fB\-\-is\-active\fR
Action: return true if specified bool token is active.
.TP
\fB\-\-get\-string\fR
Action: get string token value.
.TP
\fB\-\-activate\fR
Action: activate specified bool token.
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-string\fR
Action: set string token value.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR TOKEN_ID, \fB\-\-token\-id\fR=\fI\,TOKEN_ID\/\fR, \fB\-\-token\fR=\fI\,TOKEN_ID\/\fR
Filter only token with ID.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR TOKEN_NAME, \fB\-\-token\-name\fR=\fI\,TOKEN_NAME\/\fR
Filter only token with name.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR TOKEN_SETTING, \fB\-\-token\-setting\fR=\fI\,TOKEN_SETTING\/\fR
Filter only token with setting.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\-csv\fR=\fI\,TOKEN_CSV\/\fR
path to the token.csv file.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\-blacklist\-csv\fR=\fI\,TOKEN_BLACKLIST_CSV\/\fR
Path to token blacklist file.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Display more verbose output.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Minimize program output. Only errors and warnings are
displayed.
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\fR
Enable verbose function tracing.
.TP
\fB\-\-logconfig\fR=\fI\,LOGCONFIG\/\fR
Specify alternate config log.
.TP
\fB\-\-password\fR=\fI\,PASSWORD\/\fR
BIOS Setup password for set/activate operations.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-rawpassword\fR
Do not auto\-convert password to scancodes.
.TP
\fB\-\-memory\-dat\fR=\fI\,MEMORY_DAT\/\fR
Path to a memory dump file to use instead of real RAM
.TP
\fB\-\-cmos\-dat\fR=\fI\,CMOS_DAT\/\fR
Path to a CMOS dump file to use instead of real CMOS
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
The full documentation for
.B smbios-token-ctl
is maintained as a Texinfo manual.  If the
.B info
and
.B smbios-token-ctl
programs are properly installed at your site, the command
.IP
.B info smbios-token-ctl
.PP
should give you access to the complete manual.
